# Lead sheet and customer sheet stay together

The lead list (`/leads`, `components/leads/LeadsBoard.tsx`) and the customer list (`/kunder`, `components/customers/CustomersBoard.tsx`) are the same kind of sheet. When you change the lead sheet’s filters, date range, active-filter chips, search, export, full screen, or toolbar, apply the same change to the customer sheet in the same turn.

Shared pieces already exist. Use them on both pages instead of copying a one-off control:

- Date menu and calendar: `LeadSheetCompactDateFilter` (All time is the quiet default; the calendar opens on real record months)
- Filter dropdowns: `LeadSheetFilterMenu`
- Removable chips: `SheetFilterChipRow`
- Full screen: `LeadSheetFocusShell`, with the page title and one close icon in the header

Customers do not have a status filter. Their source filter takes that place.

The customer sheet renders won customers with the same `LeadsTable`, `leadSheet.columns`, sort, and inline-edit rules as the lead sheet. A template change must show up on both pages because both read that column list. Do not give the customer sheet a separate hardcoded column set.
